# High Noon's limit looks at the spells each player has cast this turn, whenever it entered (ruling 2024-04-12: if it
# enters on a turn where you haven't cast a spell, you can cast one that turn). Bot1 has High Noon from turn 1. On
# turn 3 Bot1 casts Flickerwisp (its one spell) exiling High Noon; with it gone Bot1 casts Mox Jet at once. At the
# beginning of the end step High Noon returns as a new object (CR 400.7): Bot1, with two spells this turn, is refused
# Lightning Bolt even with red mana ready; Bot2, who has cast nothing this turn, casts one Lightning Bolt, and is
# refused a second though it has red mana ready for it too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
High Noon
Flickerwisp
Mox Jet
Lightning Bolt
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x16

